      "content": "I'll analyze the issue and fix the workspace selection functionality.\n\n## Analysis & Pre-Thinking\n\n**Core Requirements:**\n- When a workspace is selected in `WorkspacesSection.vue`, it should open an app via the store\n- Currently, the `handleSelectWorkspaceApp` method calls `this.navigation.workspaces.open()` which doesn't trigger the proper app opening in the store\n\n**Strategic Approach:**\n1. Examine the current implementation - workspace selection uses navigation API instead of store\n2. Modify `handleSelectWorkspaceApp` to call `$storex.ui.showApp()` instead\n3. Ensure proper app parameters are passed for workspace display\n\n**Dependencies & Risks:**\n- Need to know the workspace app structure (name, component type, id)\n- The navigation API call should be replaced with store action\n- Must maintain the 'close' emit for sidebar behavior\n\n**Target Files:**\n- `src/components/layout/WorkspacesSection.vue` - Update `handleSelectWorkspaceApp` method\n\n---\n\n## File Changes\n\n```vue src/components/layout/WorkspacesSection.vue\n<script setup>\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div v-if=\"hasWorkspaceApps\" class=\"px-2 py-3 shrink-0 border-b border-white/5\">\n    <button\n      v-if=\"!isCollapsed\"\n      class=\"flex items-center justify-between w-full px-3 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-white/60 hover:text-white/80 transition-colors\"\n      @click=\"workspacesExpanded = !workspacesExpanded\"\n      title=\"Toggle Workspaces\"\n    >\n      <span>WORKSPACES</span>\n      <i :class=\"workspacesExpanded ? 'fa-solid fa-chevron-up' : 'fa-solid fa-chevron-down'\" class=\"text-xs\"></i>\n    </button>\n    <div v-if=\"workspacesExpanded || isCollapsed\" class=\"flex flex-col gap-1\">\n      <button\n        v-for=\"app in workspaceApps\"\n        :key=\"app.id\"\n        class=\"flex items-center gap-3 px-3 py-2.5 rounded-xl text-sm text-white/80 hover:bg-white/8 hover:text-white transition-colors text-left w-full\"\n        :class=\"[\n          isWorkspaceSelected(app.id) ? 'bg-white/10 text-white' : '',\n          isCollapsed ? 'justify-center' : ''\n        ]\"\n        :title=\"isCollapsed ? app.name : ''\"\n        @click=\"handleSelectWorkspaceApp(app)\"\n      >\n        <i v-if=\"app.icon\" :class=\"app.icon\" class=\"w-5 text-center shrink-0\"></i>\n        <i v-else class=\"fa-solid fa-play w-5 text-center shrink-0\"></i>\n        <span v-if=\"!isCollapsed\">{{ app.name }}</span>\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</template>\n\n<script>\nexport default {\n  props: {\n    workspaceApps: { type: Array, default: () => [] },\n    isCollapsed: { type: Boolean, default: false },\n    currentWorkspaceId: { type: String, default: null }\n  },\n  emits: ['close'],\n  data() {\n    return {\n      workspacesExpanded: false\n    }\n  },\n  computed: {\n    hasWorkspaceApps() {\n      return this.workspaceApps && this.workspaceApps.length > 0\n    },\n    navigation() {\n      return this.$storex.$router.$navigation\n    }\n  },\n  methods: {\n    handleSelectWorkspaceApp(app) {\n      this.$storex.ui.showApp({\n        tabId: `workspace-${app.id}`,\n        name: app.name,\n        component: 'workspace',\n        params: {\n          workspaceId: app.id,\n          workspaceName: app.name\n        }\n      })\n      this.$emit('close')\n    },\n    isWorkspaceSelected(workspaceId) {\n      return this.navigation.getWorkspaceId() === workspaceId\n    }\n  }\n}\n</script>\n```\n\n| File Path | Action | Component / Section | Change Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `src/components/layout/WorkspacesSection.vue` | Modify | `handleSelectWorkspaceApp` method | Replaced `this.navigation.workspaces.open()` with `this.$storex.ui.showApp()` to properly open workspace as an app with tabId, name, component, and params |\n\nThe fix ensures that when a workspace is selected, it:\n1. **Opens via the store** using `showApp()` instead of the navigation API\n2. **Creates a unique tabId** based on the workspace ID to prevent duplicates\n3. **Passes workspace parameters** properly (workspaceId, workspaceName)\n4. **Maintains the close behavior** for sidebar collapse on mobile/narrow views",
